 PARITY MAPPING (web -> native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Data        : pattern/flags/testStr useState + matches useMemo
               -> RegexTesterModel.{pattern,flags,testString} + .evaluation.
 Engine      : RegExp + global exec loop, `if (!m[0]) break`, try/catch
               -> NSRegularExpression; g=>all-vs-first, i=>.caseInsensitive,
                  m=>.anchorsMatchLines; zero-width break replicated; UTF-16
                  offset == JS m.index (NSString/NSRange are UTF-16, like JS).
 flagOptions : g / gi / gm / gim / '' (t('No Flags')) -> RegexFlagCatalog (verbatim
               labels; only the empty entry localized).
 Components  : ToolCard->inline header; Input->pattern field; Select->flags Picker;
               Textarea->TextEditor; Badge->TSBadge (shared) + token capsule.
 States      : web renders badge always + match list when length>0. Native renders
               EVERY branch (never a blank box):
                 idle           (empty pattern/test) -> friendly hint
                 invalidPattern (catch)              -> error panel  [= "error"]
                 noMatches      (valid, 0)           -> empty hint   [= "empty"]
                 matches        (>0)                 -> match list   [= "content"]
               NOTE (honest): "loading / stale / offline" are network/cache states
               with NO analog in a pure-local synchronous transform; the web source
               has none either. Documented, not silently dropped.
 i18n keys   : Regex Tester, Regex Tester Desc, No Flags, Pattern, Flags,
